# Deployment — Local Reference (not in version control)

Copy this file to `DEPLOY.md` and fill in your credentials.

## Server Details

- **Host:** ssh.example.com
- **Port:** 22
- **User:** your-ssh-username
- **SSH Key:** ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

## Directory Structure

- **App root:** `/path/to/app/`
- **Web root:** `/path/to/public_html/`
- **Branch:** `statamic`

## Connect

```bash
ssh -p PORT -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 USER@HOST
```

## Deploy

```bash
# Pull latest code
ssh -p PORT -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 USER@HOST \
  'cd /path/to/app && git pull origin statamic && php artisan statamic:stache:clear && php artisan cache:clear'

# Upload built frontend assets (run yarn build locally first)
rsync -avz -e "ssh -p PORT -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519" \
  public/build/ \
  USER@HOST:/path/to/public_html/build/

# Upload images (when public/img/uploads/ has changed)
rsync -avz -e "ssh -p PORT -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519" \
  public/img/uploads/ \
  USER@HOST:/path/to/public_html/img/uploads/
```

## Statamic CP

- **URL:** https://your-domain.com/cp
- **Email:** your-email
- **Password:** your-password

## Notes

- The web root (`public_html/`) is separate from the app root — built assets and uploaded images must be rsynced separately; git pull alone is not enough.
- `public_html/index.php` bootstraps the app using absolute paths.
- No Node/Yarn on the server — always build assets locally before deploying.
